Memoize osd_get_cache_line_size() -- it is called once per compiled DRC block.

WHAT IS WRONG UPSTREAM

drcbex64.cpp generate() (and drcbearm64.cpp) calls osd_get_cache_line_size()
unconditionally, for one purpose: the block-start alignment mask. On Linux
osdlib_unix.cpp implements it as fopen/fscanf/fclose on

    /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cache/index0/coherency_line_size

with no caching anywhere in between. So MAME opens, reads and closes a sysfs
file EVERY TIME the recompiler emits a block, to re-learn a constant. Present
since ff92d10a048.

THE CALL RATE IS NOT SMALL (measured, not assumed)

Three kernel uprobes placed by raw ELF offset on the SHIPPED, unmodified
production binary -- no instrumented build, no ptrace -- counted

    mips3_device::code_compile_block   ==   drcbe_x64::generate
                                       ==   osd_get_cache_line_size
                                       ==   syscalls:sys_enter_openat

all four exactly 12832 in the same 20 s window. Two things follow. First the
chain is 1:1:1, so this really is once per block. Second, MAME's openat count
IS its block-compile rate: in this workload the emulator opens no other file,
which makes `perf stat -e syscalls:sys_enter_openat -p <pid>` a zero-overhead
blocks-per-second meter. (Do not use `strace -c` for this. Its ptrace stops
cost 30-100 us apiece and distort both the rate and the share.)

Measured rate on indy_4610, IRIX 6.5.22, golden v3, -frameskip 6:

    regime                            blocks/s      blocks per 1e9 cycles
    cold boot, active                 3150-4400          1270-1780
    console -> iconlogin chooser       620-2670           260-1100
    settled idle 4Dwm desktop            3-11               1.4-4.6

The idle desktop compiles essentially nothing -- with the 256 MB DRC cache the
working set stops being evicted -- so this patch is worth nothing there. Boot
is where it pays, and boot is the regime that is below 100% and therefore not
clamped by the tile's throttle.

WHAT THE TRIPLE COSTS

The lab box runs IBRS + PTI + MDS "clear CPU buffers" mitigations, which is why
three syscalls are not cheap here. Two independent measurements agree:

  * a standalone microbenchmark of exactly this fopen/fscanf/fclose, pinned to
    the same core pair: 10.3-11.2 us/call, ~25 000 cycles/call;
  * inside MAME, differencing kernel cycles between the two builds over the
    same emulated window: ~33 000-38 000 cycles per call.

DIRECT EFFECT, MEASURED IN MAME (see docs/lab/irix-cache-line-size-memo.md)

cycles:k is where the whole triple lands, so the arms separate there far more
cleanly than in end-to-end speed on a shared box. Five runs per arm, arms
interleaved, one core pair, one source tree for both arms (only osdlib_unix.cpp
differed between the two links), same golden, same flags, 2.42-2.47 GHz:

    window                          stock kshare   memoized kshare   removed
    whole boot, emu 0-190 s            4.01 %          1.40 %        2.61 %
    compile-heavy phase, emu 0-70 s    5.78 %          1.73 %        4.05 %

i.e. 2.6 % of everything the emulator burns across a boot -- and 4 % of it while
the recompiler is working hardest -- was this one constant being re-read.
Per-run spread of the difference 2.28-3.05 %. Nothing measurable at the idle
desktop, as the rate table predicts. End-to-end cycnorm% could not resolve it:
the box was carrying five sibling agents at load 12-15 and foreign occupancy on
the claimed core pair reached 103 %, so the speed A/B is reported in the doc as
corroboration only, not as the claim.

The fix is one function-local static. The value cannot change while the process
lives. It is upstreamable as-is -- nothing in it is lab-specific, and it fixes
drcbearm64.cpp for free -- and should be sent to mamedev/mame.

diff --git a/src/osd/modules/lib/osdlib_unix.cpp b/src/osd/modules/lib/osdlib_unix.cpp
--- a/src/osd/modules/lib/osdlib_unix.cpp
+++ b/src/osd/modules/lib/osdlib_unix.cpp
@@ -122,17 +122,26 @@ void osd_break_into_debugger(const char *message)
 std::pair<std::error_condition, unsigned> osd_get_cache_line_size() noexcept
 {
 #if defined(__linux__)
-	FILE *const f = std::fopen("/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cache/index0/coherency_line_size", "r");
-	if (!f)
-		return std::make_pair(std::error_condition(errno, std::generic_category()), 0U);
-
-	unsigned result = 0;
-	auto const cnt = std::fscanf(f, "%u", &result);
-	std::fclose(f);
-	if (1 == cnt)
-		return std::make_pair(std::error_condition(), result);
-	else
-		return std::make_pair(std::errc::io_error, 0U);
+	// Cached: the DRC back-ends call this once per compiled block (see
+	// drcbex64.cpp generate(), drcbearm64.cpp generate()), and the value
+	// cannot change while the process is running.  Without the cache every
+	// block compiled costs an open/read/close of sysfs plus the stdio
+	// machinery around it.
+	static std::pair<std::error_condition, unsigned> const s_cached = [] () noexcept
+			{
+				FILE *const f = std::fopen("/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cache/index0/coherency_line_size", "r");
+				if (!f)
+					return std::make_pair(std::error_condition(errno, std::generic_category()), 0U);
+
+				unsigned result = 0;
+				auto const cnt = std::fscanf(f, "%u", &result);
+				std::fclose(f);
+				if (1 == cnt)
+					return std::make_pair(std::error_condition(), result);
+				else
+					return std::make_pair(std::error_condition(std::errc::io_error), 0U);
+			}();
+	return s_cached;
 #else // defined(__linux__)
 	return std::make_pair(std::errc::not_supported, 0U);
 #endif
